  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off on June 15th and a Phase 1 budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms, with a meeting scheduled for August 5th. The team expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session on September 10th, and later welcomed Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. Ideas for enhancing data visualization tools were solicited by July 20th. Following the design phase, the development phase began next month under lead developer Omar Jensen. The project reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype, and user interface enhancements are planned for October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. The project is now nearing its final stages, with all tasks expected to be completed as per the agreed timeline."
